			<div class="content" id="post-content-3586242">
									

<p>You're actually spot on. Its distance to the earth is proportionate to the distance between Earth and Sun. The change in height is proportional: Earth is, at its closest, 147,100,993km away from the Sun. Then, it moves away by, roughly, 5,000,000km. I used the relationship between those, and extrapolated that to the center of the earth to the position of the sphere. 0.03% of the distance between the center of the earth and the position of the sphere is roughly 2500 meters.</p>
<p>Do you think the article would benefit from the calculation? Some of the people I talked to figured it would not be interesting for most readers, as it doesn't add much. But the downside is that we do end up here, where you - and probably others - might be unclear on how its height/distance works.</p>

							</div>

								
