<p>Ah, I see.</p>
<p>So, my 2 suggestions then. The first one is I think absolutely necessary&#8230; The second would have clarified it for me.</p>
<p>1. Change &quot;between summer and winter&quot; to &quot;between July and January&quot;. The first one just doesn't make sense, and that's jarring. This sphere never appears in a place where it's summer. In July, it's zooming 2500m over Australian winter.</p>
<p>2. Either as a footnote on dependent or an extra sentence around there, maybe &quot;the changes in altitude of the sphere relative to the center of the Earth are directly proportional to the change in distance from the Earth to the Sun&quot;. But you can probably write it more clearly than that :) No need for the math, just explain the relationship.</p>

